.DS_Store
.env
# The HTTP cache and the 15MB players dataset are regenerable and churn
# constantly. Player headshots are neither: a photo is keyed by player id and
# does not change, so committing them is what stops the second machine
# re-downloading ten megabytes it already had. `output/headshots/` stays out —
# it is a copy of these bytes that the board rewrites on every rebuild.
data/cache/*
!data/cache/headshots/
node_modules/
players-lounge-handoff.zip
.playwright-mcp/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Rendered scenes are committed: an export costs ~18s of ffmpeg, it never
# changes once made, and a draft that moves between machines should not have to
# re-render what it already produced. `render/index.ts` names every scene
# `{draftId}-{pickNo}-{playerId}.{format}`, so the leading digit is what tells a
# real export apart from everything else that lands in output/ — ad-hoc dev
# screenshots, and the board, which is rebuilt every single pick and would
# otherwise commit a multi-megabyte blob 112 times.
output/*
!output/[0-9]*-[0-9]*-*.png
!output/[0-9]*-[0-9]*-*.gif
!output/[0-9]*-[0-9]*-*.mp4
!output/[0-9]*-[0-9]*-*.html
